If a cockatrice stones you by touching you, it takes a while (some four
turns or so, I believe). If you touch the cockatrice, though, it's your
own fault and your are immediately turned to stone. This can happen in
quite a few different ways: you can accidentally pick up a corpse bare-
handed, you can fight the cockatrice bare-handed and hit it, you can
wear gloves and eat the cockatrice' corpse, or you might be VERY
unlucky and eat an egg (cockatrices DO lay eggs: any egg you find may
be a cockatrice' egg). Lastly, you may be wielding the cockatrice'
corpse (gloved, that is), fall down stairs because you are overloaded,
and accidentally hit yourself with the corpse.

